{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CeuoTdXsxHiQPEktmPHsG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis, here are the key findings:\n\n**Repository findings at:**\n- Order.kt:11 - Order data class (no status field currently)\n- OrderController.kt:16-46 - POST /orders and GET /orders endpoints\n- OrderRepository.kt:10-27 - In-memory repository\n- ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27 - In-memory repository (no findByOrderId method)\n- ApiExceptions.kt:18-24 - ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- ApiError.kt:31-37 - ErrorCode enum\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses which are handled centrally by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Status codes: 201 for creation, 200 for success, 404 for not found, 409 for conflict\n- Error responses have envelope format: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`\n- Tests use MockMvc with status and jsonPath assertions\n\n**Affected files needed:**\n1. Order.kt - add status field\n2. OrderController.kt - add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint\n3. ShipmentRepository.kt - add findByOrderId method to support bulk updates\n4. ApiError.kt - add new ErrorCode values\n5. OrderControllerTest.kt - add tests for cancel operations\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order structure change might affect serialization\n- Must ensure all-or-nothing semantics for shipment cancellation\n- Existing tests must continue to pass\n\n**Open questions:**\n- When an order is created, should it default to ACTIVE status? (Yes, stated in requirement)\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add an `status: OrderStatus` field with enum values `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED`. New orders default to `ACTIVE`.\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 409 with no changes if any shipment is CONFIRMED\n   - Cancels all CREATED shipments and changes order to CANCELLED\n   - Succeeds (no changes) if order is already CANCELLED\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes: `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (for CONFIRMED shipments case)\n\n5. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests for:\n   - Cancelling an active order succeeds and cancels CREATED shipments\n   - Retry of cancel on already-cancelled order succeeds\n   - Cancel blocked by CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 with no changes\n   - Cancel of non-existent order returns 404\n   - GET order after cancel shows CANCELLED status\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Using a separate CancelOrderRequest DTO - Rejected: The ticket specifies just POST with no body needed (idempotent cancel by orderId alone)\n- Using repository update methods instead of direct cancellation - Rejected: Simpler to work with objects directly in memory repository\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path - Cancel active order with created shipments:*\n- Read: Order from repository (exists, status=ACTIVE)\n- Read: All shipments for order (status=CREATED)\n- Write: Order status → CANCELLED\n- Write: Each shipment status → CANCELLED\n- Return: Updated Order with CANCELLED status (200 OK)\n\n*Error case - CONFIRMED shipment present:*\n- Read: Order from repository (exists, status=ACTIVE)\n- Read: All shipments for order (any status=CONFIRMED found)\n- No writes (all-or-nothing)\n- Return: Error response (409 CONFLICT with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED)\n\n*Idempotent case - Already cancelled:*\n- Read: Order from repository (exists, status=CANCELLED)\n- No reads of shipments (skip because already cancelled)\n- No writes\n- Return: Order as-is (200 OK)\n\n*Not found case:*\n- Read: Order from repository (not found)\n- Throw ResourceNotFoundException (404 NOT_FOUND)\n\n*Prevent shipment creation on cancelled order:*\n- In ShipmentController.create, before saving shipment:\n  - Read order by orderId (needed anyway for validation?)\n  - If order status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException (409 CONFLICT)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancels_active_order_and_created_shipments` - Creates order with 2 CREATED shipments, cancels order, verifies order is CANCELLED and shipments are CANCELLED\n2. `cancel_already_cancelled_succeeds` - Creates and cancels order, cancels again, verifies no error and nothing changed\n3. `cancel_blocked_by_confirmed_shipment` - Creates order with CONFIRMED shipment, attempts cancel, verifies 409 and order stays ACTIVE\n4. `cancel_unknown_order_returns_404` - Attempts to cancel non-existent order, verifies 404 with proper error code\n5. `get_cancelled_order_shows_status` - Creates, cancels, and retrieves order, verifies status field in response\n6. `shipment_creation_rejected_for_cancelled_order` - Creates and cancels order, attempts to create shipment for it, verifies 409\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow let me implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1873,"cache_read_input_tokens":21631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1873},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"702b8a67-d436-4471-832b-7be3a1d9d816","uuid":"abd086c1-b0b1-4c2c-b5b5-8b7400246aa2","timestamp":"2026-09-10T13:01:22.496Z","request_id":"req_011CeuoTcsSUTRfrjYydzioY"}
